WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.399 --> 00:00:03.292
- They call this stretch
of the North Shore

00:00:03.292 --> 00:00:05.272
the Seven Mile Miracle.

00:00:05.272 --> 00:00:09.506
There is a world-class surf
break every 100 or so yards.

00:00:09.506 --> 00:00:13.069
We rescue up to a thousand people a year.

00:00:13.069 --> 00:00:14.276
Definitely one of the most dangerous

00:00:14.276 --> 00:00:17.109
stretches of beaches in the world.

00:00:20.569 --> 00:00:22.267
My name is Tau Hannemann

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.299
and I've been a lifeguard for 14 years

00:00:24.299 --> 00:00:26.785
here on the North Shore.

00:00:26.785 --> 00:00:29.375
I work here at Ehukai Beach Park.

00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:33.375
It's the home of the surf
break Banzai Pipeline,

00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:34.637
which is a very dangerous wave

00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:37.555
that breaks in very shallow water.

00:00:37.555 --> 00:00:39.867
It's such a critical wave
that if you fall down,

00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:41.003
the chances of getting injured,

00:00:41.003 --> 00:00:43.753
of hitting the reef is very high.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:48.855
Even when it's really small,

00:00:48.855 --> 00:00:51.835
we have very strong, powerful rip currents.

00:00:51.835 --> 00:00:54.898
It's very easy to get swept
out in the rip current

00:00:54.898 --> 00:00:58.064
and not be able to make it back to shore.

00:00:58.064 --> 00:01:02.231
Just yesterday, the lifeguards
made about 20 rescues.

00:01:06.144 --> 00:01:08.999
Knowing that the possibility
of drowning is very real,

00:01:08.999 --> 00:01:12.234
you know, especially in
large surf, we all train.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:16.207
My training consists of
running the beach or swimming

00:01:16.207 --> 00:01:18.707
anything basically in my area.

00:01:19.626 --> 00:01:20.753
We do mock rescues.

00:01:20.753 --> 00:01:22.918
If the surf is big, I'll
tell one of my partners,

00:01:22.918 --> 00:01:26.024
“hey, go out and get pounded in the surf.

00:01:26.024 --> 00:01:28.519
“I’ll come get you with the rescue tube.”

00:01:28.519 --> 00:01:30.699
So he'll go out and, you know,
he's taking waves on the head

00:01:30.699 --> 00:01:34.329
and we'll see how fast we can get to him.

00:01:34.329 --> 00:01:35.541
Whatever the ocean's going to do,

00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:38.733
if someone needs help and you
have to go get that person,

00:01:38.733 --> 00:01:41.233
you gotta be ready to do that.

00:01:44.787 --> 00:01:47.247
You're putting yourself
in a very risky situation,

00:01:47.247 --> 00:01:49.059
but knowing that your
partner has your back,

00:01:49.059 --> 00:01:52.282
it builds a strong sense of camaraderie.

00:01:52.282 --> 00:01:56.147
We have a good morale between us all.

00:01:56.147 --> 00:01:58.483
We do this job for the love of the job.

00:01:58.483 --> 00:02:01.234
Basically, if you can save
another person's life,

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.734
it's very rewarding, for sure.

